"scenario": {
"title": "The Big Bump",
"cast": [
{
"name": "Priya",
"emoji": "🧑"
},
{
"name": "Tom",
"emoji": "🧑"
},
{
"name": "Grace",
"emoji": "🧑"
},
{
"name": "Britney",
"emoji": "🐔"
}
],
"intro": "**Priya**, who runs a bakery and drives the red car; **Tom**, her flour supplier, in the blue car; **Grace**, the smiling ride attendant. BUMP! Priya's red car and Tom's blue car have crashed nose to nose. Tom supplies the flour for Priya's bakery, and things have gone sour. Let's see how they get off the rink...",
"steps": [
{
"say": [
{
"who": "Priya",
"text": "Your flour came late and I lost a whole wedding order!"
},
{
"who": "Tom",
"text": "Not my fault. I'm not going to court over this."
},
{
"who": "Priya",
"text": "You don't get a say. I'm suing."
}
],
"q": "Does Priya need Tom's agreement to start a court claim?",
"opts": [
"No. A claimant can always issue a claim, unless there is a valid arbitration agreement.",
"Yes. Both parties must agree before anyone goes to court.",
"Yes, because court hearings are private and both must consent.",
"No, and the court will always refuse to send the case anywhere else."
],
"a": 0,
"why": "No agreement is needed for litigation.",
"whys": [
"",
"That is arbitration (and mediation): both must agree. Court needs no agreement.",
"Court hearings are normally public, in open court.",
"If there is a valid arbitration agreement, the court must stay the claim (s.9)."
]
},
{
"say": [
{
"who": "Tom",
"text": "Hang on. Our contract says any dispute goes to arbitration! But Priya has already issued a court claim."
},
{
"who": "Grace",
"text": "Then don't do anything hasty, Tom. What's your first move?"
}
],
"q": "What should Tom do?",
"opts": [
"File an acknowledgment of service, then apply for a stay under s.9 before taking any step to answer the claim.",
"File his defence first, then ask for a stay.",
"Ask the judge to decide whether a stay would be a good idea.",
"Nothing: the court claim stops by itself."
],
"a": 0,
"why": "The stay is mandatory if he applies in time.",
"whys": [
"",
"Filing a defence first loses the right to a stay.",
"The court must grant the stay unless the agreement is null and void, inoperative or incapable of being performed.",
"He has to apply for the stay."
]
},
{
"say": [
{
"who": "Grace",
"text": "Before anyone races to a referee, why not try the pit lane bench? Talk it out."
},
{
"who": "Priya",
"text": "(to Tom) Shall we try mediation?\"* ... *\"Tom? Mediation?"
},
{
"who": "Tom",
"text": "(seen, no reply)"
},
{
"who": "Britney",
"text": "Silence counts as saying no, and it can cost you."
}
],
"q": "If Tom goes on to win, what is the risk of ignoring Priya's invitations?",
"opts": [
"The court may reduce or refuse his costs, because silence in response to an invitation to ADR is itself unreasonable.",
"He loses the case.",
"His claim or defence is automatically struck out.",
"None, because he never actually said no."
],
"a": 0,
"why": "The penalty is a costs sanction.",
"whys": [
"",
"The winner still wins; the penalty is a costs sanction.",
"It is a costs sanction, not strike out.",
"Silence is itself unreasonable."
]
},
{
"say": [
{
"who": "Grace",
"text": "Here's the helper. No whistle, see? She won't decide anything."
},
{
"who": "Priya",
"text": "OK... a discount on my next flour orders, and a proper apology?"
},
{
"who": "Tom",
"text": "Fine. Sorry, Priya. Ten per cent off for a year."
}
],
"q": "Who decides the outcome at a mediation?",
"opts": [
"The parties themselves; the mediator only helps them negotiate.",
"The mediator, whose decision binds both sides.",
"A judge, after reading the mediator's report.",
"An independent expert who decides the technical issue."
],
"a": 0,
"why": "The mediator does not decide and cannot impose an outcome.",
"whys": [
"",
"That describes arbitration.",
"Mediation is private and the parties decide.",
"That is expert determination."
]
},
{
"say": [
{
"who": "Tom",
"text": "Deal! Shake on it?"
},
{
"who": "Priya",
"text": "Hold on. Is it binding yet?"
}
],
"q": "When does their deal become binding?",
"opts": [
"Once they both sign a written settlement agreement.",
"As soon as they shake hands on the bench.",
"When the mediator announces the result.",
"Never: mediation can't produce a binding result."
],
"a": 0,
"why": "Nothing is binding until it is signed.",
"whys": [
"",
"Nothing is binding until a written settlement agreement is signed.",
"The mediator decides nothing.",
"The signed settlement agreement is binding."
]
}
],
"outro": {
"who": "Britney",
"text": "Priya had already issued her claim, so they can put the deal in a consent order, or keep the terms secret in a Tomlin order's confidential schedule, with liberty to apply. Off they drive, together."
},
"icon": "",
"label": "Scenario: The Big Bump"
},
